; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR LIFE RACE  -  bytecode vs native 1802   (two programs, one file)
; ==========================================================================
; Load this ONE file - VM1 at $4000, VM2 at $5000 - then cold-boot. The same Game
; of Life board (a 24 x 10 acorn) runs on both sides: VM1 on the left computes
; each generation in STELLAR bytecode, VM2 on the right in native 1802 through
; $F1 RUNMC. After 8 generations VM1 asks VM2 to stop (its RB = 2); VM2 writes
; its generation count into VM1's R5 ($D3), halts, and VM1 prints the score.
; ESC quits at any time (VM1 looks once a board row; other keys are ignored).
; Every run starts fresh (boards built in code), so it can be rerun without
; reloading.
;
; Every board row is ONE PRINTSTR of a ready-made "ESC[rr;ccH" + 24 cells string,
; so the two VMs never garble each other's output. VT100 cursor addressing only.
;
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-26 (Craig).
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/liferace_verify.py, V0061.33, two-VM cold boot): a first run booted into DIRTY board RAM and a RERUN from the memory it left (no reload) both pass and match exactly: every board drawn (VM1 generations 0-8, VM2 0-572) matches a Python Life model; VM2 did 572 generations to VM1's 8 - about 71 times as many. ESC tested: 'x' ignored, ESC mid-generation stops both VMs cleanly (VM2 halts itself, START byte intact) and a rerun after it passes in full. VM1 uses RUNNING COLUMN SUMS (~6,300 opcodes a generation, 1.83x the first version). Run time: ~36 million 1802 instructions (~3.5 min at 3 MHz) plus ~200 KB of output (~3.5 min at 9600 baud): expect about 7 minutes.
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; VM1: 305   VM2: 138 STELLAR commands (+ 180 bytes of native 1802 code).

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  VM1 ($4000): bytecode, the title, the score  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    GO = 0: VM2 waits
; D 4005 11 0C 00 00    LOADXI R12 0000                    RC = 0: VM2 has not stopped yet
; D 4009 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 400D D0 12          SHAREVM on, read/write             VM2 reads our RB, and writes our R5 and RC when it stops
; D 400F 11 0E 0E 80    LOADXI R14 0E80
; D 4013 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4015 11 0E 0E D9    LOADXI R14 0ED9
; D 4019 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 401B 11 03 0B 00    LOADXI R3 0B00
; D 401F 11 04 0E 37    LOADXI R4 0E37
; D 4023 FB 34 00       FILLMEMXY R3..R4 00                Boards A and B (and the gap between) all dead
; D 4026 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000
; D 402A 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001                        the acorn
; D 402D 2F 03 0B 72    WRITEIDX R3 0B72
; D 4031 2F 03 0B 8E    WRITEIDX R3 0B8E
; D 4035 2F 03 0B A5    WRITEIDX R3 0BA5
; D 4039 2F 03 0B A6    WRITEIDX R3 0BA6
; D 403D 2F 03 0B A9    WRITEIDX R3 0BA9
; D 4041 2F 03 0B AA    WRITEIDX R3 0BAA
; D 4045 2F 03 0B AB    WRITEIDX R3 0BAB
; D 4049 11 03 00 1B    LOADXI R3 001B
; D 404D 11 04 00 08    LOADXI R4 0008                     string index: past the header
; D 4051 11 0A 00 0A    LOADXI R10 000A
; BRi:
; D 4055 11 09 00 18    LOADXI R9 0018
; BCi:
; D 4059 2E 03 0B 00    READIDX R3 0B00
; D 405D 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 405F 2E 07 0A 60    READIDX R7 0A60                    '.' or '#'
; D 4063 2F 04 08 00    WRITEIDX R4 0800
; D 4067 42 03          INCX R3
; D 4069 42 04          INCX R4
; D 406B 43 09          DECX R9
; D 406D 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 406F A1 00 59       IFFALSEI BCi
; D 4072 52 03 00 02    ADDXI R3 0002
; D 4076 52 04 00 09    ADDXI R4 0009
; D 407A 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 407C 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 407E A1 00 55       IFFALSEI BRi
; D 4081 11 01 00 00    LOADXI R1 0000
; D 4085 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 4088 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 408C 11 08 03 E8    LOADXI R8 03E8
; D 4090 4D 78          DIVXY R7 / R8
; D 4092 25             COPYMAA
; D 4093 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4096 2F 0E 0A 13    WRITEIDX R14 0A13
; D 409A 27             COPYREMA
; D 409B 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 409D 11 08 00 64    LOADXI R8 0064
; D 40A1 4D 78          DIVXY R7 / R8
; D 40A3 25             COPYMAA
; D 40A4 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40A7 2F 0E 0A 14    WRITEIDX R14 0A14
; D 40AB 27             COPYREMA
; D 40AC 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 40AE 11 08 00 0A    LOADXI R8 000A
; D 40B2 4D 78          DIVXY R7 / R8
; D 40B4 25             COPYMAA
; D 40B5 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40B8 2F 0E 0A 15    WRITEIDX R14 0A15
; D 40BC 27             COPYREMA
; D 40BD 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 40BF 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 40C1 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40C4 2F 0E 0A 16    WRITEIDX R14 0A16
; D 40C8 11 0E 08 00    LOADXI R14 0800
; D 40CC 11 09 00 0A    LOADXI R9 000A
; SR0:
; D 40D0 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       One board row: ONE opcode, never cut
; D 40D2 52 0E 00 21    ADDXI R14 0021
; D 40D6 43 09          DECX R9
; D 40D8 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 40DA A1 00 D0       IFFALSEI SR0
; D 40DD 11 0E 0A 00    LOADXI R14 0A00
; D 40E1 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       The generation count
; D 40E3 11 0B 00 01    LOADXI R11 0001                    GO: VM2 may start drawing
; LOOP:
; D 40E7 11 03 00 1B    LOADXI R3 001B                     The first interior cell
; D 40EB 11 04 00 08    LOADXI R4 0008                     row string: past the header
; D 40EF 11 09 00 33    LOADXI R9 0033                     end of the first row
; D 40F3 11 0A 00 0A    LOADXI R10 000A
; GR0:
; D 40F7 BD 03 35       CALL ESCCHK                        Once a row: ESC quits
; D 40FA 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000                     L = the dead border column
; D 40FE 2E 03 0A E6    READIDX R3 0AE6                    M = column sum under the first cell
; D 4102 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6
; D 4104 2E 03 0B 00    READIDX R3 0B00
; D 4108 46 06          ADDAX R6
; D 410A 21 16          COPYAX MA -> R6
; D 410C 2E 03 0B 1A    READIDX R3 0B1A
; D 4110 46 06          ADDAX R6
; D 4112 21 16          COPYAX MA -> R6
; GC0:
; D 4114 2E 03 0A E7    READIDX R3 0AE7                    R = the ONE new column sum
; D 4118 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 411A 2E 03 0B 01    READIDX R3 0B01
; D 411E 46 07          ADDAX R7
; D 4120 21 17          COPYAX MA -> R7
; D 4122 2E 03 0B 1B    READIDX R3 0B1B
; D 4126 46 07          ADDAX R7
; D 4128 21 17          COPYAX MA -> R7
; D 412A 50 56 08       ADDXYZ R5 + R6 -> R8
; D 412D 50 87 08       ADDXYZ R8 + R7 -> R8               T = L + M + R: the 3 x 3 total
; D 4130 86 08 00 03    TESTXI R8 0003
; D 4134 A0 01 48       IFTRUEI GA0                        3: alive
; D 4137 86 08 00 04    TESTXI R8 0004
; D 413B A1 01 59       IFFALSEI GD0                       not 3 or 4: dead
; D 413E 2E 03 0B 00    READIDX R3 0B00                    4: as it was
; D 4142 81 00 01       TESTAI 0001
; D 4145 A1 01 59       IFFALSEI GD0
; GA0:
; D 4148 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001
; D 414B 2F 03 0D 00    WRITEIDX R3 0D00
; D 414F 10 00 23       LOADAI 0023
; D 4152 2F 04 08 00    WRITEIDX R4 0800
; D 4156 B0 01 67       GAL GN0
; GD0:
; D 4159 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 415C 2F 03 0D 00    WRITEIDX R3 0D00
; D 4160 10 00 2E       LOADAI 002E
; D 4163 2F 04 08 00    WRITEIDX R4 0800
; GN0:
; D 4167 23 00 65       COPYXY R6 -> R5                    slide: L = M
; D 416A 23 00 76       COPYXY R7 -> R6                    M = R
; D 416D 42 03          INCX R3
; D 416F 42 04          INCX R4
; D 4171 87 39          TESTXY R3 = R9
; D 4173 A1 01 14       IFFALSEI GC0
; D 4176 52 03 00 02    ADDXI R3 0002                      over the two border cells
; D 417A 52 04 00 09    ADDXI R4 0009                      the next row string
; D 417E 52 09 00 1A    ADDXI R9 001A
; D 4182 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 4184 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 4186 A1 00 F7       IFFALSEI GR0
